# --- SDD boilerplate ---
# BOILERPLATE-ONLY — every rule below exists only to keep this template's empty
# shell clean for distribution. Before real project work begins, prune this file:
#   - delete the `src-code-frontend/` / `src-code-backend/` lines once `/speccraft.scaffold`
#     has produced real source code — that code must be committed, not ignored
#   - delete or narrow the `spec/business/*`, `spec/tasks/*`, `spec/lld/*`,
#     `spec/traceability/*`, `spec/progress/*` blocks once real spec content
#     (business specs, LLDs, tasks, progress records, traceability) exists —
#     each currently keeps only its folder's README.md tracked and silently
#     ignores everything else, which is correct for an empty boilerplate and
#     wrong for a real project. See root README.md §Before You Start.
#
# SDD workflow output (per-feature generated content) — not scaffold setup.
# Keep only README.md / index files as directory scaffolding.

spec/business/*
!spec/business/README.md

spec/tasks/*
!spec/tasks/README.md

spec/lld/*
!spec/lld/README.md

spec/traceability/*
!spec/traceability/README.md
!spec/traceability/TRACEABILITY.md
!spec/traceability/shared/
!spec/business/cr-changes/

spec/progress/*
!spec/progress/README.md
!spec/progress/shared/

# generated application deliverables, not workflow setup
src-code-frontend/
src-code-backend/
# --- end SDD boilerplate ---
